    <dataIdInfo>
        <idAbs>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This feature service provides a detailed dataset compiling new and previously published geologic mapping to represent the surficial sediments across Minnesota. It focuses on the texture and genesis of these sediments, offering a comprehensive view of the state's Quaternary geology.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature Layers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Surficial Geology&lt;/strong&gt;: This layer depicts surficial sediments categorized by texture rather than provenance, using color-coded map units such as green for diamicton interpreted as till, red/orange for sand and gravel-dominated sediments, and blue for silt and clay. It incorporates glacial sediments mapped with lithostratigraphic formation names and identifies post-glacial and proglacial sediments by genesis. The dataset also includes peat and modern lake sediments, representing the most recent and detailed surficial geology data available for Minnesota.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geographic Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The data covers the entire state of Minnesota, supporting geological and environmental studies throughout the region.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use Cases&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Geological mapping and research focused on glacial and post-glacial sediment distribution.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Water resource management&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Environmental assessments and land-use planning requiring detailed surface sediment information.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure development and natural resource management benefiting from understanding sediment textures and deposit types.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This dataset is curated and provided by the Minnesota Geological Survey, with licensing encouraging appropriate citation to credit the source. The service supports GIS applications that require detailed, reliable surficial geological information for analysis and decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style='display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; max-width:1000px;'&gt;&lt;div style='align-items:center; background-color:#f7f7f7; border-radius:6px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding:8px 12px;'&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minnesota Surficial Geology Application&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a style='background-color:#7A0019; border-radius:4px; color:#fff; padding:10px;' target='_blank' href='https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/31a950366d7d43ae92f5477de5617679' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'&gt;&lt;strong&gt;View&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style='display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; max-width:1000px;'&gt;&lt;div style='align-items:center; background-color:#f7f7f7; border-radius:6px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding:8px 12px;'&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minnesota Surficial Geology Database&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a style='background-color:#7A0019; border-radius:4px; color:#fff; padding:10px;' target='_blank' href='https://mngs-umn.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/UMN::d-01-surficial-geology-of-minnesota/about' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</idAbs>
